From ff383f4b7de668a01d2cb0e9f79cbbb3b02f1b7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris <meischris39@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:51:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] RetroPlayer: Give every savestate a thumbnail and show it in
 game

A hardware-rendered frame only exists on the GPU, so savestates from
cores like Flycast showed as blank tiles. Read the published capture
back into system memory when the savestate is taken and make the
thumbnail from that copy.

The in-game saves dialog drew each savestate by loading the video frame
stored in it and rendering that through the current video filter,
stretch mode and rotation, which a hardware-rendered savestate never
had. Every savestate carried a full frame for it, the dialog ran the
shader once for each save on screen, and a save looked different there
from the dialog shown before a game starts. Show the thumbnail instead,
as that dialog does, and stop storing the video frame. Thumbnails are
made from the frame captured with the savestate, so they show the
moment the game was saved.

This removes the gamewindow control's <pixels> tag. An overwritten
savestate keeps its thumbnail's path, so the thumbnail's URL carries the
time the savestate was made, and the dialog keeps a savestate's old
thumbnail until the new one is written.
